{{/*
  gallery — the /templates gallery page shell.

  internal/server's gallery handler (phase-7 task-5) serves this page: for
  every built-in template it shows the template's name, usage (slide|section),
  one-line description, the template's example slide rendered through
  internal/render, and its field/section/body documentation
  (requirements.requirement.templates-gallery).

  It is a standalone page: OFFLINE, and — like the error page — it is a
  built-in embedded shell, not project-theme-styled: it never references the
  project's theme stylesheet, never a CDN or any network location
  (global.constraint.go-static-embedded-binary). Every colour, font and
  spacing value it uses is a neutral custom property defined inline in this
  file's own <style> block, so the page renders correctly with zero external
  CSS dependencies.

  Embedding / access:
    The pages sub-tree is embedded by internal/assets and exposed as
    assets.Pages() (an fs.FS rooted at pages/), so this file's path is
    "gallery.html.tmpl". internal/server does, in effect:

      template.Must(template.New("gallery").
          ParseFS(assets.Pages(), "gallery.html.tmpl"))

    parsing the page in its own template namespace (each page is standalone).

  Execution context (a struct or map[string]any supplying these keys):

    .Title      string   document heading and <title>. Empty falls back to
                         "Templates".
    .Subtitle   string   optional line under the heading.
    .Templates  iterable of template entries, one per registered template, in
                         the order internal/server provides (the registry's
                         sorted name order). Each entry supplies:

      .Name         string        template name, e.g. "content".
      .Usage        string        "slide" or "section".
      .Description  string        the one-line description.
      .Example      template.HTML the example slide, already rendered through
                                  internal/render (RenderSlide for a slide
                                  example); injected verbatim inside a framed
                                  preview. internal/server marks it safe.
      .Fields       iterable      the declared fields; each supplies:
          .Name        string
          .Type        string     field type, e.g. "text", "number".
          .Required    bool
          .Default     string     display form of the default, "" when none.
          .Limits      string     human display of the applied rules, e.g.
                                  "max 80 chars", "2–4 items", "≥ 0"; "" when
                                  unbounded.
          .Formats     string     named formats and the default, e.g.
                                  "compact, exact, percent (default compact)";
                                  "" when the field takes no format.
          .Description string
                                  A template with no fields may pass an empty
                                  (or nil) .Fields; the "no fields" sentence
                                  is then shown.
      .Sections     iterable      the declared sections; each supplies:
          .Name        string
          .Accepted    string     accepted section-template names, joined for
                                  display, e.g. "column".
          .Repeats     string     allowed repeat count, e.g. "2–4", "≥ 1",
                                  "any"; "" when unrestricted.
          .Description string
                                  An empty (or nil) .Sections means the
                                  template declares none.
      .Body         entry         the implied-body rule; supplies:
          .Mode        string     "required", "optional" or "disallowed".
          .Limits      string     human display of the limits, e.g.
                                  "max 2 paragraphs"; "" when unbounded.
          .Summary     string     a one-line plain-language sentence.

  Everything the template prints is html/template-escaped except .Example,
  which is already-rendered HTML marked safe by internal/server. The page
  never invents template content: it only presents what internal/server hands
  it from the registry.

  Hook slots:
    "live-reload" is a named block, exactly like the deck and error pages', so
    internal/server may override it with {{ define "live-reload" }} before
    parsing and inject its SSE client script. The gallery is static, so an
    empty block is the default.
*/}}

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>{{ with .Title }}{{ . }}{{ else }}Templates{{ end }}</title>

  {{/* This page is a built-in embedded shell (not project-theme-styled),
       so it never links the project's theme stylesheet. */}}
  <style>
    /* Self-contained: neutral custom properties defined and consumed only
       within this file, so the page renders with zero external CSS
       dependencies. */
    :root {
      --gallery-space-1: 0.25rem;
      --gallery-space-2: 0.5rem;
      --gallery-space-3: 1rem;
      --gallery-space-4: 1.5rem;
      --gallery-space-5: 2rem;
      --gallery-content-width: 90%;
      --gallery-bg: #1a1a1a;
      --gallery-fg: #f0f0f0;
      --gallery-fg-muted: #a0a0a0;
      --gallery-highlight: #ff6b6b;
      --gallery-ink: #1a1a1a;
      --gallery-border: #3a3a3a;
      --gallery-border-width: 1px;
      --gallery-radius: 0.375rem;
      --gallery-off-white: #2a2a2a;
      --gallery-font-body: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
      --gallery-font-display: var(--gallery-font-body);
      --gallery-font-heading: var(--gallery-font-body);
      --gallery-font-mono: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Consolas, "Liberation Mono", Menlo, monospace;
      --gallery-font-size-title: 1.75rem;
      --gallery-font-size-heading: 1.125rem;
      --gallery-font-size-body: 1rem;
      --gallery-font-size-small: 0.875rem;
      --gallery-line-height: 1.5;
    }
    * { box-sizing: border-box; }
    html, body { margin: 0; }
    body {
      padding: var(--gallery-space-5);
      background: var(--gallery-bg);
      color: var(--gallery-fg);
      font-family: var(--gallery-font-body);
      line-height: var(--gallery-line-height);
    }
    .gallery-page { width: var(--gallery-content-width); max-width: 72rem; margin: 0 auto; }
    .gallery-page__header { border-bottom: var(--gallery-border-width) solid var(--gallery-highlight); padding-bottom: var(--gallery-space-3); }
    .gallery-page__title {
      font-family: var(--gallery-font-display);
      font-size: var(--gallery-font-size-title);
      margin: var(--gallery-space-4) 0 var(--gallery-space-2);
    }
    .gallery-page__subtitle { margin: 0; color: var(--gallery-fg-muted); }
    .gallery-page__list { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
    .gallery-page__item {
      margin: var(--gallery-space-5) 0;
      padding: var(--gallery-space-4);
      border: var(--gallery-border-width) solid var(--gallery-border);
      border-radius: var(--gallery-radius);
    }
    .gallery-page__name { font-family: var(--gallery-font-heading); font-size: var(--gallery-font-size-heading); margin: 0; }
    .gallery-page__usage {
      display: inline-block;
      margin-left: var(--gallery-space-2);
      padding: 0 var(--gallery-space-1);
      border-radius: var(--gallery-radius);
      background: var(--gallery-highlight);
      color: var(--gallery-ink);
      font-family: var(--gallery-font-mono);
      font-size: var(--gallery-font-size-small);
      vertical-align: middle;
    }
    .gallery-page__description { margin: var(--gallery-space-2) 0 var(--gallery-space-3); color: var(--gallery-fg-muted); }
    .gallery-page__preview {
      margin: 0 0 var(--gallery-space-4);
      padding: var(--gallery-space-3);
      border: var(--gallery-border-width) dashed var(--gallery-border);
      border-radius: var(--gallery-radius);
      background: var(--gallery-off-white);
      overflow-x: auto;
    }
    .gallery-page__preview > section, .gallery-page__preview > div { margin: 0; }
    .gallery-page__docs h3 {
      font-family: var(--gallery-font-heading);
      font-size: var(--gallery-font-size-body);
      margin: var(--gallery-space-3) 0 var(--gallery-space-2);
    }
    .gallery-page__table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: var(--gallery-font-size-small); }
    .gallery-page__table th, .gallery-page__table td {
      text-align: left;
      padding: var(--gallery-space-1) var(--gallery-space-2);
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--gallery-border);
      vertical-align: top;
    }
    .gallery-page__table th { font-family: var(--gallery-font-heading); }
    .gallery-page__table code { font-family: var(--gallery-font-mono); }
    .gallery-page__empty { color: var(--gallery-fg-muted); font-style: italic; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <main class="gallery-page">
    <header class="gallery-page__header">
      <h1 class="gallery-page__title">{{ with .Title }}{{ . }}{{ else }}Templates{{ end }}</h1>
      {{ with .Subtitle }}<p class="gallery-page__subtitle">{{ . }}</p>{{ end }}
    </header>

    <ul class="gallery-page__list">
      {{ range .Templates }}
      <li class="gallery-page__item">
        <h2 class="gallery-page__name">{{ .Name }}<span class="gallery-page__usage">{{ .Usage }}</span></h2>
        {{ with .Description }}<p class="gallery-page__description">{{ . }}</p>{{ end }}

        {{/* The example slide, rendered through internal/render. */}}
        {{ with .Example }}<div class="gallery-page__preview">{{ . }}</div>{{ end }}

        <div class="gallery-page__docs">
          <h3>Fields</h3>
          {{ if .Fields }}
          <table class="gallery-page__table">
            <thead>
              <tr><th>Field</th><th>Type</th><th>Required</th><th>Default</th><th>Rules</th><th>Formats</th><th>Description</th></tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              {{ range .Fields }}
              <tr>
                <td><code>{{ .Name }}</code></td>
                <td>{{ .Type }}</td>
                <td>{{ if .Required }}yes{{ else }}no{{ end }}</td>
                <td>{{ with .Default }}{{ . }}{{ else }}—{{ end }}</td>
                <td>{{ with .Limits }}{{ . }}{{ else }}—{{ end }}</td>
                <td>{{ with .Formats }}{{ . }}{{ else }}—{{ end }}</td>
                <td>{{ .Description }}</td>
              </tr>
              {{ end }}
            </tbody>
          </table>
          {{ else }}
          <p class="gallery-page__empty">This template declares no fields.</p>
          {{ end }}

          <h3>Sections</h3>
          {{ if .Sections }}
          <table class="gallery-page__table">
            <thead>
              <tr><th>Section</th><th>Accepts</th><th>Repeats</th><th>Description</th></tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              {{ range .Sections }}
              <tr>
                <td><code>{{ .Name }}</code></td>
                <td><code>{{ with .Accepted }}{{ . }}{{ else }}—{{ end }}</code></td>
                <td>{{ with .Repeats }}{{ . }}{{ else }}any{{ end }}</td>
                <td>{{ .Description }}</td>
              </tr>
              {{ end }}
            </tbody>
          </table>
          {{ else }}
          <p class="gallery-page__empty">This template declares no sections.</p>
          {{ end }}

          <h3>Body</h3>
          {{ with .Body }}
          <p>{{ .Summary }}{{ with .Limits }} ({{ . }}){{ end }} — <code>{{ .Mode }}</code>.</p>
          {{ else }}
          <p class="gallery-page__empty">—</p>
          {{ end }}
        </div>
      </li>
      {{ else }}
      <li class="gallery-page__item"><p class="gallery-page__empty">No templates are registered.</p></li>
      {{ end }}
    </ul>
  </main>

  {{/* Phase-7 live-reload client script is injected here by internal/server. */}}
  {{ block "live-reload" . }}{{ end }}
</body>
</html>
